   "description": "The threat for very heavy rainfall and significant flash flooding is\nincreasing across west central Texas mainly Tuesday night through\nThursday. The combination of the remnants of Hurricane Polo from the\nPacific, abundant tropical moisture and a cold front will result in\nperiods of very heavy rainfall which may produce localized\nsignificant flash flooding. Looks like the heaviest rainfall will\nset up mainly east of a Sweetwater to Ozona line with widespread\n2 to 3 inches. Isolated totals of around 10 inches are not out of\nthe question by Thursday evening mainly east of a Coleman to\nSonora line",
